{"version":"activity-event.v1","id":"AEV-260829-c85388912130816d01c37c0e","sequence":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-29T22:23:46.790186Z","actor":{"principal":{"availability":"unknown"},"agent":{"availability":"known","value":"claude"},"run":{"availability":"unknown"},"session":{"availability":"known","value":"cd6863d1-aba8-4d24-b557-d30776243ffe"},"operator":{"availability":"unknown"}},"subject":{"element_id":"STORY-260830-2mj14b","element_type":"story"},"source":{"kind":"local_cli","entrypoint":"cmd.runMutate","request":{"availability":"unknown"}},"correlation_id":"COR-260829-61fe9b8880ab02b10c270255","causal_order":1,"operation":"content","changes":[{"field":"scope","before":{"kind":"text","text":"(define story scope)"},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"agents-infra local-model profiles and model-harness. Downstream of the llama.cpp migration decision: this makes engines interchangeable, it does not itself pick one. Deployed defaults change only when a separate decision says so."}},{"field":"acceptance_criteria","before":{"kind":"text","text":"(define acceptance criteria)"},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"A local-model profile names model, environment and engine independently; a canonical knob set — context bound, prefill chunk, reasoning effort, output bound, sampler — is translated per engine rather than spelled by the caller; and adding an engine does not require touching callers or relaxing any comparison-gate admission clause."}}]}
{"version":"activity-event.v1","id":"AEV-260829-41f25c6e12179319a9bdab75","sequence":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-29T22:28:00.946556Z","actor":{"principal":{"availability":"unknown"},"agent":{"availability":"known","value":"claude"},"run":{"availability":"unknown"},"session":{"availability":"known","value":"cd6863d1-aba8-4d24-b557-d30776243ffe"},"operator":{"availability":"unknown"}},"subject":{"element_id":"STORY-260830-2mj14b","element_type":"story"},"source":{"kind":"local_cli","entrypoint":"cmd.runMutate","request":{"availability":"unknown"}},"correlation_id":"COR-260829-9ad5bae4bc25bb389c4950d5","causal_order":1,"operation":"content","changes":[{"field":"scope","before":{"kind":"text","text":"agents-infra local-model profiles and model-harness. Downstream of the llama.cpp migration decision: this makes engines interchangeable, it does not itself pick one. Deployed defaults change only when a separate decision says so."},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"Do NOT build a second plugin system here. skill-agents-management already owns the agentic-system and vendor plugin layers and documents a planned local-model plugin with load/unload awareness, inference-busy state and memory-pressure sequencing. The inference-engine axis belongs there, and agents-infra becomes a consumer alongside task-board so extension happens in one place."}},{"field":"acceptance_criteria","before":{"kind":"text","text":"A local-model profile names model, environment and engine independently; a canonical knob set — context bound, prefill chunk, reasoning effort, output bound, sampler — is translated per engine rather than spelled by the caller; and adding an engine does not require touching callers or relaxing any comparison-gate admission clause."},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"The inference engine is a first-class configurable axis implemented as a local-model plugin layer in skill-agents-management, with agents-infra consuming it rather than carrying its own engine handling, so adding an engine touches one repository."}}]}
